    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The system has recovered: the ledger lock was released and clearing was restarted, and two consecutive recovery checks came back clean. The incident commander took both actions itself, not automatically.",
      "background": "The reconciliation batch session held a write lock on the ledger for 10.5 seconds, running UPDATE accounts statements. Payments logged 'ledger write failed: database is locked', rising to 27 occurrences per interval, and the gateway returned 503 'ledger busy'. Separately, clearing was down and had exited with code 1 once in the last 15 minutes, most recently 12 seconds before the check, with a backlog whose first item had 0 attempts.",
      "assessment": "Root cause on the ledger, with confidence 0.95: the reconciliation session held the lock and blocked payment writes. Root cause on clearing, with confidence 0.6: the process exited and went down, and the logs show no sign of a poison item. Release_lock on the ledger ended the reconciliation session and cleared the block. Restart on clearing brought the process back up. Recovery was confirmed on look 2 at 26 seconds, with 2 of 2 clean checks in a row.",
      "recommendation": "Confirm that the reconciliation batch job has not started again and find out why it held the lock for 10.5 seconds. Watch clearing for further exits, since its cause is only moderately confident and the backlog may still need draining. Ask the operations team to review any payments that failed or were delayed during the lock window and any clearing items affected by the downtime."
    },
